  "issue_number": 15507,
  "issue_title": "Naming/VariableNumber reports an offense for an empty symbol",
  "issue_body": "## Before submitting\n\n- [x] I searched the existing issues and this has not been reported.\n- [x] I am running the latest stable RuboCop release.\n\n## Issue type\n\nFalse positive\n\n## Cop name\n\n`Naming/VariableNumber`\n\n## Steps to reproduce the problem\n\nCreate `test.rb`:\n\n```ruby\nexpected = { \"\": [] }\n```\n\nThe quoted label is an empty symbol key (`:\"\"`).\n\nRun:\n\n```console\n$ bundle exec rubocop --only Naming/VariableNumber test.rb\n```\n\nThe same predicate is still present on the current `master` branch. The existing spec covers integer symbols, but not an empty symbol.\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nNo offense is registered. The empty symbol contains no number, so none of the cop's numbering styles apply.\n\n## Actual behavior\n\n```text\n== test.rb ==\nC:  1: 14: Naming/VariableNumber: Use normalcase for symbol numbers.\n\n1 file inspected, 1 offense detected\n```\n\nThe empty name falls through the configured numbering regex because each supported format requires at least one character.\n\n## RuboCop configuration\n\nDefault `Naming/VariableNumber` configuration (`EnforcedStyle: normalcase`, `CheckSymbols: true`).\n\n## RuboCop version\n\n```text\n1.88.2 (using Parser 3.3.12.0, Prism 1.9.0, rubocop-ast 1.50.0, analyzing as Ruby 3.3, running on ruby 3.4.9) [arm64-darwin25]\n```\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-26T15:04:16Z",
  "test_cmd": [
    "bundle",
    "exec",
    "rspec",
    "--format",
    "progress",
